<p>Use the NSW Design System to create customer-centred digital products and services that meet branding and WCAG 2.2 AA accessibility guidelines. It also helps you meet the <a class="nsw-link nsw-link--icon" target="_blank" href="https://www.digital.nsw.gov.au/digital-service-toolkit/design-standards" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Design Standards (opens in a new tab)"><span>Design Standards</span><span class="material-icons nsw-material-icons" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true">open_in_new</span></a> to design for user needs</p>
<p>The NSW Design System provides an adaptable and extensible base that includes:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Foundations</strong> – core visual and structural styles that communicate the NSW Government identity.</li>
  <li><strong>Components</strong> – reusable interface elements with guidance for consistent, accessible implementation.</li>
  <li><strong>Utility classes</strong> – single-purpose helpers for common spacing, layout, visibility and styling needs.</li>
  <li><strong>Methods</strong> – best-practice design guidance for common user tasks and service problems.</li>
</ul>

